      "writtenOn": "2024-11-11T06:16:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s related to HCI flow control (Vol 4, Part E 4 HCI FLOW CONTROL).\n\nWe can send several packets depending on the buffer size of the controller, if it\u0027s full we should wait for the HCI_Number_Of_Completed_Packets response.\n\nThe reason why we have `number_of_sent_packets_` is that we should assume unsent packets are flushed when a connection is disconnected. \n\n`one packet` is a bit ambiguous because one L2CAP packet can be split into multiple \u0027HCI packets\u0027 depending on the controller settings. \n`one fragment` \u003d\u003d `one HCI packet`.",
      "parentUuid": "8f7c0a68_ffb7146e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 220,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 220,
        "endChar": 53
